# Optional. Without it the app runs unchanged and simply reports nothing.
#
# Where monitoring beacons are sent — errors, and timings that exceeded their
# budget. Never card content, never a spreadsheet id. Leave it unset unless you
# have somewhere to receive them, such as a Cloudflare Worker.
#
# Traffic and Core Web Vitals do not come through here: those are Cloudflare
# Web Analytics, turned on in the dashboard, which sets no cookie and no
# identifier. That is the only source for LCP, INP and CLS — the app carries no
# vitals code of its own, because two sources for one number is one too many
# and this was the one that cost bytes.
VITE_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT=

# Optional but strongly recommended. The absolute origin the site is served
# from. Without it og:url stays relative, and the canonical link and sitemap.xml
# are not emitted at all — a canonical has to be absolute to mean anything, and
# a sitemap entry that is not absolute is invalid.
#
#   VITE_SITE_ORIGIN=https://sokki.example.workers.dev
#
# It is not a secret — it is the address people type — but it is a property of
# a deployment rather than of this code, so it is set on Cloudflare rather than
# committed: a fork that inherited it would point its canonical at this site.
# Set it here to build a local copy that carries the same URLs.
#
# A build on Cloudflare without it fails rather than shipping a page with no
# canonical; a local build only warns.
VITE_SITE_ORIGIN=

# Cloudflare Web Analytics, installed in the page rather than at the edge.
#
# Automatic injection is zone-level: it lands on every hostname under the
# domain, so a project on a subdomain has its numbers mixed into the parent's.
# Web Analytics also will not offer automatic setup for a subdomain, because a
# "site" there means a zone. Installing the snippet ourselves reports only where
# this build is served.
#
# Empty means no beacon is emitted at all, which is what a local build wants.
VITE_CF_BEACON_TOKEN=
